<title>AUSTRALIA: Blueberry year earnings hopes squashed.</title>
<headline>Blueberry year earnings hopes squashed.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Blueberry Farms of Australia Ltd said on Monday its earnings for the year to June 30, 1997 will be significantly lower than expected earlier this year.</p>
<p>The downgrade flowed from lower than expected production and litigation over alleged non-payment of an indemnity debt.</p>
<p>Blueberry, which floated in 1995, said lower production was caused mainly by declining productivity in older plantings.</p>
<p>It expected 1997/98 earnings to be affected by further declining production from older bushes -- moderated by new plantings -- and the on-going litigation.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
